'' '##_' AT THE END OF A MACRO BODY JOINS THE NEXT END OF LINE TO REACH THE OUTPUT,
'' and the substitution loop is not where that can be decided. The rule was armed as an
'' engine flag while PpSubstitute walked the body -- ahead of any of the body being
'' emitted -- so a body of TWO lines whose second ends in '##_' ate the separator
'' between line one and line two and kept the invocation's. One statement was split
'' where fbc joins, and the split fell inside a declaration:
''
''     #macro BEGIN_ENTRIESMAP()
''     function _GetMapEntries( ) as _MAP_ENTRY ptr
''         static as _MAP_ENTRY _entries(0 to ...) = { ##_
''     #endmacro
''
'' left 'static ... = {' alone on its line, so the array was never declared, and
'' 'return @_entries(0)' then read '_entries' as a call to an unknown function.
'' pp/token-pasting.bas:141 and :144, its last two declines. The join is a MARKER in
'' the token stream now (TF_JOIN_MARK) and EmitTok arms it in output order.
''
'' MEASURED AGAINST fbc, and this file's own output matches fbc's byte for byte:
''
''   fbc -r on the declaration emits a STATICALLY INITIALISED DATA OBJECT and nothing
''   at run time --
''       static struct $10_MAP_ENTRY _ENTRIES$1[4] = {{1,2},{3,4},{5,6},{0,0}};
''       static struct $8FBARRAY1I10_MAP_ENTRYE tmp$2$1 =
''           { _ENTRIES$1, _ENTRIES$1, 64, 16, 1, 49, {{ 4, 0, 3 }} };
''   -- no zeroed static, no construction loop, no guard flag and no atexit thunk.
''   HANDOFF's group 11 says this shape "needs a zeroed static plus a construction
''   loop, which this path cannot express"; that is true only of a ctor-bearing
''   element type. _MAP_ENTRY is two integers, fbc constructs nothing, and the
''   declaration was never what declined here.
''
''   THE ELLIPSIS BOUND IS RESOLVED BY COUNTING THE BRACE LIST: four elements give
''   '[4]' and a descriptor of ELEMENTS 4, LBOUND 0, UBOUND 3.
''
''   The four neighbouring shapes -- the ellipsis bound on a non-static local and on a
''   module-level 'dim shared', and an explicit bound either way -- all lowered
''   already, before this change. They are kept in the source so that a regression in
''   the initialiser path is told apart from one in the join.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/line-join-body.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' GOLDEN: expected/line-join-body.out
